From f1ccb8b0215d4ade7c7c6bd971030e1bf7b7fb18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saman-amd <saman-amd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rocsparse): null COO store in csr2hyb_kernel on gfx1151

csr2hyb_template allocates the HYB COO arrays only when the host-side
coo_nnz is greater than zero, but csr2hyb_kernel does not read coo_nnz.
It re-derives per-row overflow from csr_row_ptr, so whenever the host
decided there was no COO part while the kernel found a row longer than
ell_width, the kernel stored through a null pointer:

  Memory Fault Error [GPU index: 0, faulting addr: 0x0,
    kernel: void rocsparse::csr2hyb_kernel<512u, float>(...)]
  Memory access fault by GPU node-1 on address (nil).
    Reason: Page not present or supervisor privilege.

The existing coo_row_ind null test only guarded the coo_idx computation,
leaving the three stores in the else branch unguarded. Gate those stores
on the same predicate so the kernel can never write to an array that was
not allocated.

Why this is carried as a patch: the fix belongs in rocm-libraries, but it
aborts all three rocsparse shards of the gfx1151 test suite today, so it
is carried here until the upstream change merges and the submodule is
bumped past it. See ROCm/TheRock#6472.

Reproduction (gfx1151, rocsparse-test built from the submodule):

  HIP_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1 ./rocsparse-test --gtest_filter=\
    'quick/copy_info.auxiliary/f32_r_37_37_NT_rand:\
     quick/copy_info.auxiliary/f32_r_37_37_T_rand'

Both tests pass individually; the fault needs the pair. Without this
change 7 of 10 runs abort with the fault above, with it 10 of 10 report
"[  PASSED  ] 2 tests.". Running the wider *csr2hyb*:*hyb*:*copy_info*
filter aborts after 1315 tests unpatched and completes past 1551 patched.

diff --git a/projects/rocsparse/library/src/conversion/csr2hyb_device.h b/projects/rocsparse/library/src/conversion/csr2hyb_device.h
index 2529588b5d8..bde6996b9eb 100644
--- a/projects/rocsparse/library/src/conversion/csr2hyb_device.h
+++ b/projects/rocsparse/library/src/conversion/csr2hyb_device.h
@@ -87,7 +87,11 @@ namespace rocsparse
 
         rocsparse_int row_begin = csr_row_ptr[ai] - idx_base;
         rocsparse_int row_end   = csr_row_ptr[ai + 1] - idx_base;
-        rocsparse_int coo_idx   = coo_row_ind ? workspace[ai] - idx_base : 0;
+
+        // The COO arrays are only allocated when the host determined that some
+        // row overflows ell_width. Nothing may be stored through them otherwise.
+        const bool    has_coo = (coo_row_ind != nullptr);
+        rocsparse_int coo_idx = has_coo ? workspace[ai] - idx_base : 0;
 
         // Fill HYB matrix
         for(rocsparse_int aj = row_begin; aj < row_end; ++aj)
@@ -99,7 +103,7 @@ namespace rocsparse
                 ell_col_ind[idx]  = csr_col_ind[aj];
                 ell_val[idx]      = csr_val[aj];
             }
-            else
+            else if(has_coo)
             {
                 // Fill COO part
                 coo_row_ind[coo_idx] = ai + idx_base;
-- 
